    294 +6. Add one coordinator and one worker with no sensitive privileges.
    295 +7. Add secrets, persistence, health checks, backup, and resource limits one at a time.
    296 +8. Decide whether the long-term agent “OS” remains immutable OCI desired state or moves into a NixOS VM.
    297 +
    298 +## Confidence and known unknowns
    299 +
    300 +- **High confidence:** Fedora-native rootless Quadlet is supported by the installed host and is the shortest path to a working service.
    301 +- **High confidence:** Nix can reproducibly build OCI archives that Fedora Podman consumes without making the host NixOS.
    302 +- **High confidence:** a minimal, standalone, flake-pinned Home Manager configuration can safely manage only selected files if collision checks and build-before-switch are respected.
    303 +- **Moderate confidence until tested:** the exact agent application image, writable paths, SELinux labeling, health check, and UID mapping; these depend on the actual agent runtime.
    304 +- **Low confidence / not recommended:** treating a privileged Podman container as a fully autonomous NixOS machine. Use a VM if those semantics are truly required.
    305 +
